# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug
target

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/

# Ignore localized Markdown docs except README variants and user docs in docs/
**/*_RU.md
**/*_ru.md
!**/README_RU.md
!**/README_ru.md
!docs/**/*_RU.md
!docs/**/*_ru.md
TASKS.md

# AI-facing and internal working docs — kept local, never published
AI_CONTEXT*
AI_RULES*
ARCHITECTURE*
CLAUDE*
LESSONS_LEARNED*
TECHNICAL*
OLD_TASKS_RU*
# Deferred feature-design backlog — local only for now
FEATURES*
# Internal design documents: they describe HOW a mechanism works inside, which
# belongs in notes/, not in the published tree.
*_DESIGN.md

# Local environment overrides
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.cargo-home/
.cargo/

# Local user-only runtime data
configs/local/
presets/local/

# Book notes — local only, not for the repo
notes/

# For errors files for coding agents
errors/

# Captured runtime output. The service's own logs live under `errors/` and in
# %ProgramData%, but a log or an NDJSON dump copied next to the sources for a
# quick look carries hostnames, addresses and process names — never publish one
# by accident.
*.log
*.ndjson

# VS Code local settings
.vscode/
.history/
*.code-workspace

# Editor and IDE state
.idea/
.vscode/
.codex/
.claude/
# Visual Studio's own workspace state: a multi-megabyte content index, a
# SQLite browse database and per-user window layout. Local by nature.
.vs/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Qt / Qt Creator local files and generated artifacts
*.pro.user
*.pro.user.*
*.pri.user
*.qbs.user
CMakeLists.txt.user
.qmake.stash
cmake-build-*/
build-*/
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
# An in-tree CMake/packaging output directory. `build-*/` above only catches
# the suffixed variants; a plain `build/` or `dist/` next to the sources is one
# stray `-B build` away.
/build/
/dist/
**/build/CMakeCache.txt
Makefile.Debug
Makefile.Release
object_script.*.Debug
object_script.*.Release
moc_*.cpp
moc_*.h
qrc_*.cpp
ui_*.h
*.qmlc
*.jsc
*.qrc.depends

# Developer scripts. The default is "internal" — task-list migrations and other
# one-offs that only make sense against this checkout's own bookkeeping. The
# exceptions below are tools anyone working on the code can reuse.
# The pattern excludes the directory's CONTENTS, not the directory: git cannot
# re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded.
scripts/dev/*
!scripts/dev/probe_hosts.py
!scripts/dev/merge-duplicate-locale-keys.py
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Conflict copies left by the file-sync client next to the original.
# scripts/clean-sync-duplicates.* deletes them; this keeps one from being committed.
* (2).*
* (3).*
* (4).*
